  "functions": [
    "FUNC.SLOPE"
  ],
  "kind": "bit-matching-detail",
  "title": "SLOPE pairs known_y's then known_x's, skips non-numeric positions, and centers with two-pass means",
  "statement": "In Excel 16.0 builds 20131 and 20527, SLOPE(known_y's, known_x's) validates singletons in formula order (returning #VALUE! for a single blank reference before inspecting the other argument), returns #N/A on shape mismatch, skips positions where either argument holds text, logical, or blank, and computes sum((x - mean_x)*(y - mean_y)) / sum((x - mean_x)^2) from two-pass sample means, returning #DIV/0! when fewer than 2 numeric pairs exist or sum((x - mean_x)^2) == 0. Matches 2,860/2,860 full-bank and 4/4 pinned rows.",
  "status": "measured",
  "basis": "Measured across Excel 16.0 build 20131 (4/4 pinned rows, oc1-oc4) and 20527 (prefix_metadata row 206, 2,860/2,860 full-bank SLOPE rows).",
